---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { Code } from 'astro:components'
import { SpecResults } from '@cypress-design/react-spec-results'
import SpecResultsCancelable from './SpecResultsCancelable'

export const frontmatter = { title: 'SpecResults', order: 4 }

const tocHeadings = [
  { depth: 2, slug: 'usage', text: 'Basic usage' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'states', text: 'Component states' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'props', text: 'Props' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'interaction', text: 'Interaction' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'purpose', text: 'When to use it' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'guidelines', text: 'Guidelines' },
]

const usageSnippet = `import { SpecResults } from '@cypress-design/react-spec-results'

export function RunOverview({ run }) {
  return (
    <SpecResults
      results={{
        failed: run.totalFailed,
        errored: run.totalErrored,
        passed: run.totalPassed,
        skipped: run.totalSkipped,
        cancelled: run.totalCancelled,
        running: run.totalRunning,
        queued: run.totalQueued,
      }}
      onCancel={run.status === 'RUNNING' ? () => cancelRun(run.id) : undefined}
    />
  )
}`
---

<BaseLayout title="SpecResults" tocHeadings={tocHeadings} rawContent={true}>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="max-w-[780px] pb-6 border-b border-gray-100 mb-0">
    <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[2px] text-purple-500 font-semibold mb-[14px] m-0">Patterns · Cypress Cloud</p>
    <h1 class="font-brand-heading font-semibold text-[56px] leading-[1.04] m-0 mb-[18px] text-gray-1000">
      SpecResults, <em class="italic text-gray-700 font-medium">the run progress at a glance.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="text-[18px] leading-[1.55] text-gray-700 max-w-[680px] m-0 mb-7">
      The run's headline in one row: how many specs failed, errored, passed, skipped, and how many
      are still to come. Each count links into the Specs tab filtered to that status, and a bar
      along the bottom edge shows the same breakdown as proportion. While the run is live it
      carries the Cancel run action.
    </p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-6 items-center text-sm text-gray-600">
      <span class="inline-flex items-center h-7 px-3 border border-gray-100 rounded-full bg-white text-sm text-purple-500 font-brand-mono">
        @cypress-design/react-spec-results
      </span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Basic usage -->
  <h2 id="usage" class="font-brand-heading font-semibold text-[30px] mt-16 mb-2 text-gray-1000">Basic usage</h2>
  <p class="text-base text-gray-700 max-w-[680px] mb-7 m-0">
    Pass per-status counts. The component hides empty statuses, applies a fixed order, and derives
    singular/plural copy. Pass <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">onCancel</code> only while the run is <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">RUNNING</code>.
  </p>
  <div class="border border-gray-100 rounded-t bg-gray-25 px-6 py-6">
    <SpecResultsCancelable
      client:only="react"
      results={{ failed: 1, passed: 18, skipped: 1, running: 2, queued: 3 }}
    />
  </div>
  <Code
    code={usageSnippet}
    lang="tsx"
    theme="github-dark"
    class="block rounded-b font-brand-mono text-sm leading-[1.6] px-5 py-4 mb-6"
  />

  <!-- Component states -->
  <h2 id="states" class="font-brand-heading font-semibold text-[30px] mt-16 mb-2 text-gray-1000">Component states</h2>
  <p class="text-base text-gray-700 max-w-[680px] mb-7 m-0">
    Everything is derived from the spec statuses and whether <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">onCancel</code> is passed. Statuses appear in a fixed
    order — failed, errored, passed, skipped, remaining — and a status with a count of zero is not
    rendered at all.
  </p>
  <div class="border border-gray-100 rounded bg-gray-25 px-6 py-8 flex flex-col gap-8 mb-4">
    <div>
      <div class="font-brand-heading text-sm leading-5 font-medium text-gray-900 mb-3">Running :: spec count not yet known</div>
      <SpecResultsCancelable client:only="react" results={{}} />
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="font-brand-heading text-sm leading-5 font-medium text-gray-900 mb-3">Running :: nothing finished yet</div>
      <SpecResultsCancelable client:only="react" results={{ running: 4, queued: 20 }} />
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="font-brand-heading text-sm leading-5 font-medium text-gray-900 mb-3">Running :: partial results</div>
      <SpecResultsCancelable
        client:only="react"
        results={{ failed: 1, passed: 18, skipped: 1, running: 2, queued: 3 }}
      />
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="font-brand-heading text-sm leading-5 font-medium text-gray-900 mb-3">Running :: all passing so far</div>
      <SpecResultsCancelable client:only="react" results={{ passed: 22, running: 2 }} />
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="font-brand-heading text-sm leading-5 font-medium text-gray-900 mb-3">Running :: scheduled to complete</div>
      <SpecResults
        client:only="react"
        results={{ failed: 1, passed: 28, skipped: 2 }}
        scheduledToComplete="60s"
      />
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="font-brand-heading text-sm leading-5 font-medium text-gray-900 mb-3">Run completed :: all specs passed</div>
      <SpecResults client:only="react" results={{ passed: 31 }} />
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="font-brand-heading text-sm leading-5 font-medium text-gray-900 mb-3">Run completed :: with failed specs</div>
      <SpecResults client:only="react" results={{ failed: 1, passed: 28, skipped: 2 }} />
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="font-brand-heading text-sm leading-5 font-medium text-gray-900 mb-3">Run completed :: with errored specs</div>
      <SpecResults
        client:only="react"
        results={{ failed: 2, errored: 3, passed: 15, skipped: 1 }}
      />
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="font-brand-heading text-sm leading-5 font-medium text-gray-900 mb-3">Removed specs label with <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-white px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded border border-gray-100">label=""</code></div>
      <SpecResults
        client:only="react"
        results={{ failed: 1, passed: 28, skipped: 2 }}
        label=""
      />
    </div>
  </div>

  <table class="w-full border-collapse bg-white border border-gray-100 rounded overflow-hidden text-base mb-4">
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td class="font-brand-mono text-sm w-[200px] font-medium py-3 pr-4 border-b border-gray-100 align-top">Running</td>
        <td class="text-gray-700 py-3 pl-4 border-b border-gray-100 align-top"><code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">running</code> or <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">queued</code> is above zero. A trailing "N specs remaining" pill sums both; the Cancel run button is shown when <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">onCancel</code> is passed. Queued specs have no pill of their own — they appear only in the bar and the remaining count.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="font-brand-mono text-sm w-[200px] font-medium py-3 pr-4 border-b border-gray-100 align-top">Scheduled to complete</td>
        <td class="text-gray-700 py-3 pl-4 border-b border-gray-100 align-top">Every group has finished but the run is held open by the project's completion delay in case more parallel groups arrive. Results are final-looking, and the trailing pill switches from a spec count to a time — "60s remaining", with the running spinner — and links to the project's General settings where the delay is configured. The bar keeps a small running block at its end so the run still reads as live. 60s is the project default. Don't pass <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">onCancel</code> here — cancelling would stamp a finished run as cancelled.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="font-brand-mono text-sm w-[200px] font-medium py-3 pr-4 border-b border-gray-100 align-top">Complete</td>
        <td class="text-gray-700 py-3 pl-4 border-b border-gray-100 align-top">Nothing running or queued and no scheduled delay. The remaining pill and Cancel button disappear.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="font-brand-mono text-sm w-[200px] font-medium py-3 pr-4 border-b border-gray-100 align-top">Just started</td>
        <td class="text-gray-700 py-3 pl-4 border-b border-gray-100 align-top">Only the remaining pill renders until the first spec finishes.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="font-brand-mono text-sm w-[200px] font-medium py-3 pr-4 border-b border-gray-100 align-top">Status mapping</td>
        <td class="text-gray-700 py-3 pl-4 border-b border-gray-100 align-top">The caller folds Cloud's instance enum into the <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">results</code> keys: <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">TIMEDOUT</code> → errored, <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">NOTESTS</code> → skipped, <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">CANCELLED</code> → cancelled, <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">UNCLAIMED</code> → queued. <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">skipped</code> and <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">cancelled</code> stay separate inputs — the component sums them into one combined "skipped" pill.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="font-brand-mono text-sm w-[200px] font-medium py-3 pr-4 border-b border-gray-100 align-top">Singular</td>
        <td class="text-gray-700 py-3 pl-4 border-b border-gray-100 align-top">A count of 1 drops the trailing "s": "1 failed spec", "1 spec remaining".</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="font-brand-mono text-sm w-[200px] font-medium py-3 pr-4 align-top">Indeterminate</td>
        <td class="text-gray-700 py-3 pl-4 align-top">Every count at zero (no spec isolation, or nothing claimed yet). Falls back to a single "Testing in progress" pill and a fully animated bar.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <!-- API -->
  <h2 id="props" class="font-brand-heading font-semibold text-[30px] mt-16 mb-2 text-gray-1000">Props</h2>
  <p class="text-base text-gray-700 max-w-[680px] mb-7 m-0">
    Presentational. Takes plain counts rather than Cloud's instance list, so it knows nothing about
    the data model. Needs no project or run identifiers; navigation is relative and cancellation is
    handed back to the caller.
  </p>
  <div class="mb-4">
    <div class="mb-16">
      <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-2 py-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center text-purple-500 mb-3">results</code>
      <div>
        <div class="flex gap-6 py-3 border-t border-b border-gray-100">
          <div class="w-[100px] shrink-0 font-brand-heading text-sm font-medium text-gray-1000">Description</div>
          <div class="text-gray-700 flex-1">Object with <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">failed</code>, <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">errored</code>, <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">passed</code>, <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">skipped</code>, <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">cancelled</code>, <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">running</code>, <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">queued</code> as numbers. Omitted keys are zero. <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">skipped</code> and <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">cancelled</code> combine into one pill.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-6 py-3">
          <div class="w-[100px] shrink-0 font-brand-heading text-sm font-medium text-gray-1000">Type</div>
          <div class="flex-1"><code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">SpecResultCounts</code></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mb-16">
      <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-2 py-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center text-purple-500 mb-3">onCancel</code>
      <div>
        <div class="flex gap-6 py-3 border-t border-b border-gray-100">
          <div class="w-[100px] shrink-0 font-brand-heading text-sm font-medium text-gray-1000">Description</div>
          <div class="text-gray-700 flex-1">When present, renders the Cancel run button and fires on click. Omit once the run completes.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-6 py-3">
          <div class="w-[100px] shrink-0 font-brand-heading text-sm font-medium text-gray-1000">Type</div>
          <div class="flex-1"><code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">() ⇒ void</code></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mb-16">
      <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-2 py-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center text-purple-500 mb-3">scheduledToComplete</code>
      <div>
        <div class="flex gap-6 py-3 border-t border-b border-gray-100">
          <div class="w-[100px] shrink-0 font-brand-heading text-sm font-medium text-gray-1000">Description</div>
          <div class="text-gray-700 flex-1">Remaining delay, e.g. <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">"60s"</code> (the project default). When set and nothing is running or queued, the remaining pill shows this time instead of a spec count.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-6 py-3">
          <div class="w-[100px] shrink-0 font-brand-heading text-sm font-medium text-gray-1000">Type</div>
          <div class="flex-1"><code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">string</code></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-2 py-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center text-purple-500 mb-3">label</code>
      <div>
        <div class="flex gap-6 py-3 border-t border-b border-gray-100">
          <div class="w-[100px] shrink-0 font-brand-heading text-sm font-medium text-gray-1000">Description</div>
          <div class="text-gray-700 flex-1">Noun appended to each pill ("28 passed specs"). Singular is derived by dropping the trailing "s". Pass <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">""</code> when the list below is already titled "Specs", so pills read "28 passed".</div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-6 py-3 border-b border-gray-100">
          <div class="w-[100px] shrink-0 font-brand-heading text-sm font-medium text-gray-1000">Type</div>
          <div class="flex-1"><code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">string</code></div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-6 py-3">
          <div class="w-[100px] shrink-0 font-brand-heading text-sm font-medium text-gray-1000">Default</div>
          <div class="flex-1"><code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">"specs"</code></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 max-w-[680px] m-0">
    React only for now — Vue is a planned fast-follow.
  </p>

  <!-- Interaction -->
  <h2 id="interaction" class="font-brand-heading font-semibold text-[30px] mt-16 mb-2 text-gray-1000">Interaction</h2>
  <p class="text-base text-gray-700 max-w-[680px] mb-7 m-0">
    Every pill is a link to the Specs tab filtered to that status, so the summary doubles as
    navigation.
  </p>
  <table class="w-full border-collapse bg-white border border-gray-100 rounded overflow-hidden text-base mb-4">
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td class="font-brand-mono text-sm w-[200px] font-medium py-3 pr-4 border-b border-gray-100 align-top">Pill click</td>
        <td class="text-gray-700 py-3 pl-4 border-b border-gray-100 align-top">Navigates route-relatively to <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">specs?specStatus=[…]</code>. The errored pill filters on <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">ERRORED</code> + <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">TIMEDOUT</code>, skipped on <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">NOTESTS</code> + <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">CANCELLED</code>, remaining on <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">RUNNING</code> + <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">UNCLAIMED</code>. Works from any tab under <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">/projects/:id/runs/:id/</code>.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="font-brand-mono text-sm w-[200px] font-medium py-3 pr-4 border-b border-gray-100 align-top">Scheduled pill</td>
        <td class="text-gray-700 py-3 pl-4 border-b border-gray-100 align-top">Links to <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">../../settings/general</code>, where the run completion delay lives — the old notice's "Manage" link.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="font-brand-mono text-sm w-[200px] font-medium py-3 pr-4 border-b border-gray-100 align-top">Pill hover</td>
        <td class="text-gray-700 py-3 pl-4 border-b border-gray-100 align-top">Text and icon take on the status's own hue rather than a generic link color, so the hover reads as "go to this status".</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="font-brand-mono text-sm w-[200px] font-medium py-3 pr-4 border-b border-gray-100 align-top">Cancel run</td>
        <td class="text-gray-700 py-3 pl-4 border-b border-gray-100 align-top">Fires <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">onCancel</code>. The component doesn't confirm or disable itself — the caller owns that flow.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="font-brand-mono text-sm w-[200px] font-medium py-3 pr-4 border-b border-gray-100 align-top">Bar</td>
        <td class="text-gray-700 py-3 pl-4 border-b border-gray-100 align-top">Not interactive. It's the same breakdown as the pills drawn as proportion; the running block animates while the run is live, and queued specs are left as empty track (gray-100 at 50% opacity) so progress is legible without color.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="font-brand-mono text-sm w-[200px] font-medium py-3 pr-4 align-top">Narrow widths</td>
        <td class="text-gray-700 py-3 pl-4 align-top">Below <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">576px</code> of the strip's own width (a container query, not the viewport) the pills and Cancel button stack vertically.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <!-- When to use it -->
  <h2 id="purpose" class="font-brand-heading font-semibold text-[30px] mt-16 mb-2 text-gray-1000">When to use it</h2>
  <p class="text-base text-gray-700 max-w-[680px] mb-7 m-0">
    SpecResults sits at the top of the Run Details tabs and answers "how is this run going?" before
    anyone scrolls. While a run is in progress it appears on every tab as a breakdown of that
    progress; once the run completes it stays only on the Specs tab, where it serves as the
    overview of the list below. It exists so the run's headline — what failed, what's left —
    doesn't have to be reconstructed by scanning the spec list. It is not a general-purpose
    progress bar: the statuses, order, and copy are fixed to Cypress Cloud's spec lifecycle.
  </p>
  <table class="w-full border-collapse bg-white border border-gray-100 rounded overflow-hidden text-base mb-4">
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td class="font-brand-mono text-sm w-[200px] font-medium py-3 pr-4 border-b border-gray-100 align-top">Running state</td>
        <td class="text-gray-700 py-3 pl-4 border-b border-gray-100 align-top">Every tab on the Run Details page(s), with <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">onCancel</code>. A breakdown of the run's progress.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="font-brand-mono text-sm w-[200px] font-medium py-3 pr-4 align-top">Completed state</td>
        <td class="text-gray-700 py-3 pl-4 align-top">Specs tab only, as the overview of the list below. Pass <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">label=""</code> there since the list is already titled "Specs".</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <!-- Guidelines -->
  <h2 id="guidelines" class="font-brand-heading font-semibold text-[30px] mt-16 mb-2 text-gray-1000">Guidelines</h2>
  <p class="text-base text-gray-700 max-w-[680px] mb-4 m-0">
    Use it once per tab, at the top. Don't add a separate progress bar or "N of M complete" line —
    the component already carries both.
  </p>
  <p class="text-base text-gray-700 max-w-[680px] mb-7 m-0">
    Pass <code class="font-brand-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 px-1 rounded border border-gray-100 inline-flex items-center h-5 text-purple-500">onCancel</code> only while the run can actually be cancelled. A disabled cancel on a finished run is chrome with no job.
  </p>

</BaseLayout>
